+### The debugger in a bugfix
+
+In a bugfix, the agent diagnoses the defect from the running program before it
+edits source: it reproduces the failure, launches the reproduction under the
+harness `debug` tool, reads the values at a breakpoint near the suspected fault,
+and writes those observed values into the diagnosis. The conductor's skill and
+`aidlc-developer-agent` both say so. While the active intent's scope is
+`bugfix`, the adapter also writes a derived rule,
+`aidlc/.aidlc-sessions/harness/rules/aidlc-debug-first.md`, that holds each
+session's first source edit until the defect has been observed (the harness
+injects a rule once per session, so the retried edit goes through). Sessions
+pick it up when they start, so it reaches the agents a bugfix dispatches.
+
+Python needs `debugpy` in the project's `.venv` (the harness looks for `python`
+there first); Node uses the JavaScript debug adapter, native code lldb or gdb,
+Go `dlv`. When no adapter applies, the agent says so in the diagnosis. In the
+bugfix scope the plan-approval fence is off, so the debugger also runs during
+Code Generation planning.
+
 ## Alongside Claude Code
 
 One project can carry both distributions: run `aidlc config --harness claude`
